Z||000004||Archie||12-26-2001||08:30 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by voyagerspe:<BR><B>I keep frying my belt on my v8 fiero.<BR>yes I have air, and all the pullys are lined up.  Ive already changed the altenator and tested the new one "underload".  Any ideas???<BR>p.s. im using a 41013 belt</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If you are using one of my kits that belt needs to be 15/32" wide. The belt you are using is 41.0" long and 13/32" wide (41013).<P>While the length of 41.0" is fine (I actually use 41.5" long) the width of 13/32" is too narrow and the "V" belt is touching bottom in the A/C or Alt. pulley.<P>Archie <P>------------------<BR>Just how fast do you want to go?<p>[This message has been edited by Archie (edited 12-26-2001).]||||reg||1
